==Trivia==
*While not available as a standalone spell in Clash of Clans, The Log reappears there in a few situations.
**The Log appears to be one of the logs launched from the Siege Machine, the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Log_Launcher Log Launcher].
**The Log is used as a trap in the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Clan_Capital Clan Capital], the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Log_Trap Log Trap].
*The Log is the cheapest {{Rarity|Legendary}} [[Cards|card]], costing 2 [[Elixir]].
*It is 1 of 3 [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] which can only be placed in the player's own territory, the others being [[Royal Delivery]] and [[Barbarian Barrel]].
*In the Italian, Dutch, Arabic, and Portuguese language settings of the game, The Log's name translates to "The Trunk". In the Japanese, Persian, and Indonesian language settings of the game, The Log's name translates to "Rolling Wood", "Timber", and "The Wood" respectively.
*The Log bears more than a passing resemblance to [https://kirby.fandom.com/wiki/Splinter Splinter] from the Kirby series.
*The Log can be seen in the menu picture for [[Arenas|Builder's Workshop]] in the bottom left corner. Before The Log was introduced into the game, it had no spikes on it.
*The Log can be seen on the [[Trophies|Trophy Road]] as a decoration.
*In [[Pass Royale|Logmas Arena]], The Log can be seen in the left side of the Arena as a decoration, resembling a Clashmas Tree.
*When deployed, you can hear a voice chanting “''LOG''”.
**The Log is 1 of 3 spells that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being [[Goblin Curse]] and [[Party Rocket]].
*The Log is featured in non-Clash games. More specifically:
**Although not available as a spell, The Log is featured as [https://brawlstars.fandom.com/wiki/Spike?file=Spike_Skin-Logmas.png a character skin for Spike] in Brawl Stars.
**Although not available as a spell, The Log reappears as [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Greg Greg]'s active ability in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*The [[Lumberjack]] is responsible for creating The Log, which is hinted at on several different occasions:
**The Lumberjack's description states ''"and hunts The Log by night"''.
**In The Log's card description, it states the cause of its creation was "''a spilt bottle of Rage''", which is a property exclusive to the Lumberjack.
**In the Clash of Clans [https://youtu.be/O__Lo2FQJKo?si=-HOvOgWxC1jNOeI- No More Clashmas?! commercial], The Log had a flashback to its creation where the Lumberjack is seen spilling the Rage spell in a forest.
**By an [[Emotes|Emote]] where the Lumberjack cowers because The Log towers over him.
**In the Clash-A-Rama episode "[https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/%22%27Twas_The_Night_Before_Clashmas%22 Twas The Night Before Clashmas]", the Kings search for a Clashmas Tree. They ignore the Lumberjack's majestic one, and decides on a smaller and ugly looking tree. The agitated Lumberjack tries to destroy it, but slips and drops his Rage spell, which converts the tree into The Log. 
*According to [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L6grys552go&list=WL&index=26&pp=gAQBiAQB TV Royale], the number of times The Log was used in [[Basics of Battle|battles]] in 2018 was 39 billion.
*The Log is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Log is the subject of a few Emotes.
**The Log is the subject of a few [[King's Tower|Tower Skins]].
*The Log was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|decks]] of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Log was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/1fuCnNBTqBU?feature=share King's Cup Tournament], by a player called TMD YAOYAO.
**The Log was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/psZXKWHkKkE?si=PbjvbZt8stghz6eJ King's Cup II Tournament], by a player called Surgical Goblin.
**The Log was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/C5qBcdcErfM?si=e37mhAgNKAA5kMJI Clash Royale League 2018 Tournament], by a player called Lciop.
**The Log was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/nMANpDweTA4?si=nsUAou7ny3WAA2ve Clash Royale League 2022 Tournament], by a player called Mohamed Light.
* There used to be a glitch where if a [[Bomb Tower]] was directly in front of the King's Tower and was hit by The Log, the Bomb Tower would extend The Log's effective range, causing it to activate the King's Tower.
*If a [[Monk]] activates Pensive Protection in the corner of the Arena, then an opposing The Log will be deflected out of the Arena's bounds.
*On 27/3/2023, a [[Training Camp|Trainer]] was added to the game called Boss Cheddar, and used a Level 18 The Log in their deck, despite the highest Level being Level 14 at the time. This Trainer was removed on 18/4/2023.
*The Log has had balance changes that were planned for it but were not added to the game. More specifically:
**The initial balance change for The Log on the [[Version History#Balance Changes (7/6/2022)|7/6/2022 balance changes]] was a pushback range decrease to 0.5 tiles (from 1 tile), but it was changed to a Crown Tower Damage decrease to 20% (from 30%) [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-36-balance-wip last minute].
**The initial balance change for The Log on the [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/3/2025)|4/3/2025 balance changes]] was a Crown Tower damage decrease to 10% (from 20%), but it was raised to 15% [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-69-balance-wip-march-2025 last minute].
**The initial balance change for The Log on the [[Version History#Balance Changes (8/7/2025)|8/7/2025 balance changes]] was a 9% damage decrease, but it was lowered to 8% [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-73-balance-wip-july-2025 last minute].

